5. ACCESSIBILITY (cited against /home/darrell/work/agents2/ACCESSIBILITY.md) — PASS

A-4 Keyboard / A-5 Visible focus — PASS. The sort trigger is a real
  `<button type="button" data-sort-btn="...">` inside each <th>
  (filemanager.html:1339, 1347, 1355, 1363). There is NO click handler on a
  bare <th>: wireButtons binds only to `[data-sort-btn]` (line 570), which is
  the button. Native <button> is Tab-reachable and fires click on both Enter
  and Space, so no key handling is needed. Focus styling is
  `focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-500`.
  I checked that `outline: none` has an equal-or-better replacement that will
  actually render: base.html:18 loads `https://cdn.tailwindcss.com`, the Play
  CDN, which generates utilities on demand at runtime — so the
  `focus-visible:ring-*` classes are not at risk of being purged out of a
  precompiled stylesheet. Ring appears only for keyboard focus, which is the
  intended focus-visible behavior.

A-7 Real table semantics — PASS. Still a `<table>`; every header retains
  `<th scope="col">` (1338, 1346, 1354, 1362, and the trailing actions column
  at 1370). No div-grid substitution. The button was nested INSIDE the th
  rather than replacing it, so the header cell's column association is intact.

A-9 Never color-only — PASS. Sort state is programmatically determinable:
  renderIndicators (532-555) sets `aria-sort="ascending"|"descending"` on the
  active th and calls `th.removeAttribute('aria-sort')` on every other th, so
  exactly one header ever carries it. The arrow is not the sole carrier. The
  glyph span is `aria-hidden="true"` in the markup (1342, 1350, 1358, 1366) and
  is only ever mutated via textContent, so it stays hidden from AT.

A-2 Both themes — PASS. Every class added ships a dark counterpart:
  `text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-900 dark:hover:text-gray-100`.
  The arrow inherits the button's color, so it is visible on the light
  `bg-gray-50` and dark `bg-gray-900/50` thead in turn. The indigo-500 focus
  ring reads against both header backgrounds.

A-15 Target size — PASS, at the boundary. `inline-flex items-center px-1
  py-0.5` with text-sm gives 20px line-height + 4px padding = 24px height,
  meeting WCAG 2.2 2.5.8's 24x24 minimum exactly; width far exceeds it. Worth
  noting as no-margin rather than comfortable, but it is not a violation.

A-13 Empty states — PASS, preserved. The `{{else}}` branch (1405-1409) still
  renders the calm "No CSV files found." row, and it carries no data-name, so
  applySort's `tbody.querySelectorAll('tr[data-name]')` (519) correctly excludes
  it from sorting instead of shuffling it among data rows.

A-14 does not apply — its "Project-specific" section describes the swarm
  dashboard, and the brief scopes this check to the numbered baseline. For the
  record P13 added no inline event-handler attributes.

A-1 (axe run) is not part of my dispatched remit as checker-tests and requires
  a live server; it belongs to checker-a11y. I flag it as not-run-by-me rather
  than claim it.

